From: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xdg-mime: query the file type with gio in generic mode

Desktops xdg-utils does not know (COSMIC) run the generic backend, which
needs `mimetype` (Perl File::MimeInfo) or `file` to find a file's type, so
`xdg-open FILE` failed on an image that ships neither. GLib's `gio info`
reads the shared-mime-info database -- the one the desktop itself uses --
so prefer it when it is installed.

Upstream: not submitted
---
--- a/scripts/xdg-mime.in
+++ b/scripts/xdg-mime.in
@@ -128,7 +128,10 @@
 
 info_generic()
 {
-    if mimetype --version >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    if gio help info >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+        DEBUG 1 "Running gio info \"$1\""
+        gio info "$1" 2> /dev/null | grep standard::content-type | cut -d' ' -f4
+    elif mimetype --version >/dev/null 2>&1; then
         DEBUG 1 "Running mimetype --brief --dereference \"$1\""
         mimetype --brief --dereference "$1"
     else
